cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the ideas in it, please cite the thesis below."
title: "Knowledge-Graph-Constrained Personalized Learning Path Recommendation with Dual-State Execution and Rolling Replanning"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for generating learning paths that are strictly legal
  on a MOOC knowledge graph (soft prompt constraints plus token-level hard
  constraints from a prefix tree), repairing paths during execution according to
  a dual-state learner profile (cognitive readiness and affective load), and
  replanning across rounds with a stability regulariser. Includes experiment
  scripts, committed outputs, and an offline demo platform.
